Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.47,0:00:03.98,sign_12_1_August_27th__Ste,,0,0,0,,{\fad(489,477)}August 27th, Stellar Year 2148
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.95,0:00:04.97,Main Top,S,0,0,0,,All right. If we have to. Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.38,0:00:08.75,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Was that Kino's group?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.10,0:00:09.97,Main,S,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.35,0:00:13.31,Main,S,0,0,0,,They looked hard, but they said \Nthey can't find Chise's Juggernaut.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.72,0:00:17.00,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Not even a little piece of it, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.00,0:00:19.71,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Well, after that artillery blast...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.07,0:00:20.95,Main,S,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.74,0:00:24.71,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,I'm sure it's not bothering you, \Nbut I'll say it anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.58,0:00:27.40,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,It's not your fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.67,0:00:34.98,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,I thought they'd come after our base next, \Nbut they haven't.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.34,0:00:39.34,Main,S,0,0,0,,Today's attack had a secondary goal \Nof testing that new weapon.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.66,0:00:41.56,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,We lost four to a "secondary goal," huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.90,0:00:44.08,Main,S,0,0,0,,If it's completed, \Nwe'll lose a lot more than four.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.08,0:00:45.62,Main,S,0,0,0,,The Republic will fall.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.14,0:00:49.92,Main,S,0,0,0,,That doesn't matter to us, \Nbut I doubt the Major will agree.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.27,0:00:52.17,Main,S,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.17,0:00:53.84,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.27,0:00:57.93,Main,S,0,0,0,,Either way, the new one's\N still silent, for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.93,0:00:58.87,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,You can tell?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.87,0:01:00.40,Main,S,0,0,0,,I memorized its voice.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.71,0:01:04.78,Main,S,0,0,0,,And I doubt the enemy commander\N will let them use it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.08,0:01:08.21,Main,S,0,0,0,,I found him.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.39,0:01:09.66,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Your brother?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.66,0:01:11.46,Main,S,0,0,0,,He found me, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.72,0:01:13.35,Main,S,0,0,0,,He'll come for me next.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.89,0:01:17.87,Main,S,0,0,0,,It's good luck for me, \Nbut bad for all of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.35,0:01:19.49,Main,S,0,0,0,,What will you do?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.86,0:01:22.73,Main,S,0,0,0,,Hang yourself tonight, \Nbefore you die tomorrow?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.37,0:01:26.33,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Not a chance in hell.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.33,0:01:30.44,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,We'll follow you to the end, Reaper.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.62,0:03:05.20,Flashback_Italics,S,0,0,0,,We're going to be wiped out.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.56,0:03:08.63,Flashback_Italics,S,0,0,0,,This unit is an execution ground.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.83,0:03:12.01,Italics,L,0,0,0,,Special orders...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.01,0:03:15.24,Italics,L,0,0,0,,Target: The deepest part \Nof Legion-held territory.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.24,0:03:18.15,Italics,L,0,0,0,,Mission duration: Unlimited. \NNo support...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.51,0:03:21.71,Italics,L,0,0,0,,Immediate execution in the event of retreat?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.29,0:03:25.81,Flashback_Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,The point of this place is \Nto make the soldiers fight until they die.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.81,0:03:28.35,Flashback_Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,This is the last place we'll serve.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.90,0:03:31.70,Flashback_Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,We'll all die here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.13,0:03:37.55,Main,A,0,0,0,,What's wrong, Lena?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.57,0:03:46.08,sign_5337_42_August_28th__Ste,A,0,0,0,,{\fad(1,480)}August 28th, Stellar Year 2148
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.84,0:03:47.96,Main Top,A,0,0,0,,A final mission with a survival rate of 0%, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.29,0:03:52.73,Main,A,0,0,0,,I guess that sounds like this country.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.73,0:03:54.69,Main,L,0,0,0,,Please, help me!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.69,0:03:56.02,Main,L,0,0,0,,I need to do something!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.02,0:03:56.91,Main,A,0,0,0,,"Do something"?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.19,0:03:58.87,Main,A,0,0,0,,Do what, specifically?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.09,0:04:00.79,Main,A,0,0,0,,Go on TV and give a speech?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.79,0:04:02.77,Main,A,0,0,0,,Find somebody important and yell at them?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.77,0:04:07.24,Main,A,0,0,0,,If that would change minds, this never \Nthings wouldn't be like this in the first place.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.03,0:04:11.51,Main,A,0,0,0,,Give it up. We can't fix this.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.51,0:04:14.00,Main,A,0,0,0,,Nothing we do matters, so just—
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.00,0:04:15.05,Main,L,0,0,0,,Stop it!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.72,0:04:18.78,Main,L,0,0,0,,Stop pretending to be a bad person \Njust to have an excuse to do nothing!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.18,0:04:22.15,Main,A,0,0,0,,You're the one who needs to stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.94,0:04:26.20,Main,A,0,0,0,,Stop...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.83,0:04:29.60,Main,A,0,0,0,,I mean it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.60,0:04:31.08,Main,A,0,0,0,,There's nothing we can do!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.08,0:04:35.93,Main,A,0,0,0,,We can't do a thing to save them!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.18,0:04:41.22,Main,L,0,0,0,,Annette...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.50,0:04:45.49,Main,A,0,0,0,,Our next-door neighbors were scientists \Non my dad's research team.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.49,0:04:47.83,Main,A,0,0,0,,Our families were close.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.83,0:04:50.65,Main,A,0,0,0,,But that all changed when the war started.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.23,0:04:56.72,Main,A,0,0,0,,They were Eighty-Six.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.89,0:04:59.88,Main,A,0,0,0,,Two boys.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.88,0:05:05.06,Main,A,0,0,0,,The older brother was way older, \Nbut the younger was my age.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.06,0:05:08.44,Main,A,0,0,0,,We went to the same school \Nand played a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.26,0:05:10.74,Main,A,0,0,0,,We were friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.96,0:05:17.24,Main,A,0,0,0,,But the next thing I knew, \Nthe Eighty-Six all stopped coming to school.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.24,0:05:20.47,Main,A,0,0,0,,And my classmates were bullying me.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.47,0:05:24.19,Main,A,0,0,0,,They said I was friends \Nwith a filthy colored.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.89,0:05:29.34,Main,A,0,0,0,,It hurt! There wasn't \Nanything I could do!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.34,0:05:33.52,Main,A,0,0,0,,But he didn't know anything\N about it and still wanted to play.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.88,0:05:36.26,Main,A,0,0,0,,I turned him down, \Nand we got in a fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.80,0:05:39.40,Main,A,0,0,0,,And I said it...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.40,0:05:41.08,Flashback,A,0,0,0,,You filthy colored!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.79,0:05:46.10,Main,A,0,0,0,,I was scared.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.46,0:05:49.49,Main,A,0,0,0,,I was scared of myself \Nfor being capable of saying that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.07,0:05:52.24,Main,A,0,0,0,,So...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.24,0:05:57.25,Main,A,0,0,0,,When my dad was thinking about\N taking them in, despite the danger,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.25,0:05:58.55,Main,A,0,0,0,,I said I didn't want to.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.96,0:06:03.84,Main,A,0,0,0,,I said he wasn't my friend. \NI said I wouldn't put myself in danger for him.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.38,0:06:07.76,Main,A,0,0,0,,I think my dad wanted my support.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.20,0:06:10.96,Main,A,0,0,0,,But I gave him a way out.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.95,0:06:16.46,Main,A,0,0,0,,They were sent to the camps \Nthe next day.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.14,0:06:21.92,Main,A,0,0,0,,All I could do was tell myself \NI couldn't do anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.92,0:06:23.72,Main,A,0,0,0,,That there was never a chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.60,0:06:28.38,Main,A,0,0,0,,But you... You always...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.35,0:06:32.04,Main,A,0,0,0,,Listen, Lena.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.04,0:06:35.24,Main,A,0,0,0,,You may act like a saint,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.76,0:06:38.81,Main,A,0,0,0,,but you're just as guilty as me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.80,0:06:50.90,Main,L,0,0,0,,What is this place?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.90,0:06:56.05,Main,A,0,0,0,,The kids who lived next door, \Nand their mother, had a strange power.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.51,0:07:00.31,Main,A,0,0,0,,They could tell what each other felt \Nwithout speaking.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.90,0:07:03.48,Main,A,0,0,0,,My dad took an interest in that power.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.29,0:07:06.83,Main,A,0,0,0,,This is where it began.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.70,0:07:11.78,Main,A,0,0,0,,First, they'd put on \Nthese little toy-like devices,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.78,0:07:15.68,Main,A,0,0,0,,and try to guess what their mom \Nwas thinking behind the curtain.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.68,0:07:17.84,Main,A,0,0,0,,The experiments were like a game.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.11,0:07:20.87,Main,A,0,0,0,,But when the military found out \Nthat there was
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.87,0:07:24.02,Main,A,0,0,0,,a new kind of communication \Nthat could replace wireless,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.02,0:07:26.85,Main,A,0,0,0,,they ordered my dad to perfect it, \Nno matter what the cost.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.53,0:07:30.35,Main,A,0,0,0,,And the result...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.08,0:07:33.46,Main,A,0,0,0,,was the RAID device you're wearing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.46,0:07:39.09,Main,A,0,0,0,,How many Eighty-Six do you think\N died to make it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.80,0:07:44.28,Main,A,0,0,0,,It shares words. \NYou can't use animals, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.28,0:07:44.73,Main,L,0,0,0,,You don't mean—
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.73,0:07:46.94,Main,A,0,0,0,,That's right. Human experimentation.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.94,0:07:50.22,Main,A,0,0,0,,Even though they said \Nthe Eighty-Six aren't human.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.22,0:07:52.28,Main,A,0,0,0,,Convenient, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.80,0:07:54.99,Main,A,0,0,0,,All the test subjects were children.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.99,0:07:57.86,Main,A,0,0,0,,Results first. Safety last.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.18,0:08:00.33,Main,A,0,0,0,,They all died suffering.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.75,0:08:05.16,Main,A,0,0,0,,My dad couldn't take it. \NHe committed suicide.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.64,0:08:07.29,Main,L,0,0,0,,It wasn't an accident?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.29,0:08:10.71,Main,A,0,0,0,,You think my dad of all people \Nwould screw up the settings on a Para-RAID?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.15,0:08:16.51,Main,A,0,0,0,,He always told me that he'd abandoned his friends \Nand caused so many deaths.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.51,0:08:19.23,Main,A,0,0,0,,He deserved to suffer and die \Nmore than anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.41,0:08:25.15,Main,A,0,0,0,,Which means I'm just as guilty \Nfor abandoning my friend, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.15,0:08:28.60,Main,A,0,0,0,,So I took over the research my dad did, \Nvictims and all!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.33,0:08:32.20,Main,A,0,0,0,,"Undertaker," was it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.80,0:08:36.80,Main,A,0,0,0,,We got the request to investigate \Nbecause of the dead Handlers, remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.80,0:08:37.66,Main,,0,0,0,,Yeah...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.66,0:08:40.78,Main,A,0,0,0,,If I'd had them bring the Processor \Nthat was the cause,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.78,0:08:43.79,Main,A,0,0,0,,I might've been able to save him, \Nif nobody else.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.46,0:08:46.39,Main,A,0,0,0,,But that's just hypocrisy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.39,0:08:49.76,Main,A,0,0,0,,I'm glad those shitheads in Transport refused.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.76,0:08:52.47,Main,A,0,0,0,,See? Nothing we can do.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.47,0:08:54.84,Main,A,0,0,0,,I can't save anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.34,0:08:58.42,Main,A,0,0,0,,But you're no different!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.20,0:09:01.00,Main,A,0,0,0,,You're even worse!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.51,0:09:06.88,Main,A,0,0,0,,You interfered and kept them alive, \Nand now they're being ordered to die!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.79,0:09:09.86,Main,A,0,0,0,,If you'd just slacked off and let them die,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.86,0:09:12.76,Main,A,0,0,0,,they wouldn't have gotten that order.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.79,0:09:15.74,Main,A,0,0,0,,And now they will, thanks to you!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.98,0:09:24.53,Main,A,0,0,0,,I hate you, Lena.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.60,0:09:27.60,Main,A,0,0,0,,Never let me see you again.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.00,0:09:45.95,Flashback,L,0,0,0,,I won't let them die.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.95,0:09:49.70,Flashback,L,0,0,0,,I won't let anyone else die.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.16,0:10:06.66,sign_14462_141_September_10th__,L,0,0,0,,{\fad(484,472)}September 10th, Stellar Year 2148
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.60,0:10:10.17,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,What do you want?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.17,0:10:14.69,Main,L,0,0,0,,Let me cancel the special recon orders \Ngiven to Spearhead!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.97,0:10:19.12,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,I told you not to get too involved.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.12,0:10:20.37,Main,L,0,0,0,,This is insane!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.37,0:10:23.43,Main,L,0,0,0,,Must they keep marching into enemy territory\N until they're dead, for no reason?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.34,0:10:27.20,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,The Eighty-Six all need to die.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.27,0:10:30.86,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,That's what's best for the country,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.86,0:10:33.79,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,according to its government, \Nand indirectly, its people.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.16,0:10:37.28,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,That's the will of the nation.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.99,0:10:44.13,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,If what we've done to the Eighty-Six\N gets out at the end of the war,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.13,0:10:47.44,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,the Republic will become a pariah state
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.44,0:10:50.79,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,and remembered forever as oppressors.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.54,0:10:54.06,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,And to keep that from happening...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.06,0:10:57.76,Main,L,0,0,0,,And that's why you forbid them \Nfrom recovering or burying their dead?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.22,0:11:02.04,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,When they're all dead, \Nthey will cease to have existed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.28,0:11:07.59,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,And thus, the Republic\N will have done nothing wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.59,0:11:11.15,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,A very small number know the exact truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.15,0:11:13.81,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,But the vast majority who look the other way,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.81,0:11:15.91,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,or just don't care, are supporters of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.76,0:11:22.52,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,And our job as the army, Lena, \Nis to follow the people's wishes!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.25,0:11:26.19,Main,L,0,0,0,,The Eighty-Six are part of the Republic as well!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.37,0:11:30.96,Main,L,0,0,0,,The Republican ideals that Saint Magnolia\N expounded should protect them, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.96,0:11:33.76,Main,L,0,0,0,,If they aren't, how can this \Nbe the will of the Republic?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.22,0:11:38.34,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,It's a country full of fools and villains,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.34,0:11:43.55,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,who executed Saint Magnolia for the \Nsake of their own wealth and greed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.13,0:11:46.49,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,What can you expect of them?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.51,0:11:55.02,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,Humans were not ready\Nto have freedom and equality.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.50,0:11:57.40,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,And I think we'll ever be.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.76,0:12:01.40,Main,L,0,0,0,,You're just saying that \Nto justify your despair!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.40,0:12:04.18,Main,L,0,0,0,,It's wrong to sit back \Nand let this happen!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.18,0:12:07.41,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,You're free to speak of your hopes and ideals,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.41,0:12:09.31,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,but you won't persuade anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.16,0:12:12.94,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,That's why you came to me, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.46,0:12:17.33,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,Hope and despair are the same thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.33,0:12:19.18,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,You want something, and you can't have it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.82,0:12:23.59,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,They're two names \Nfor two sides of the same thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.73,0:12:34.05,Main,L,0,0,0,,Captain Nouzen, \NI have a set of special recon orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.05,0:12:35.46,Italics,S,0,0,0,,I've received them.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.61,0:12:37.87,Main,L,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.19,0:12:41.54,Main,L,0,0,0,,I couldn't do anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.74,0:12:43.22,Italics,S,0,0,0,,I'm sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.65,0:12:47.25,Main,L,0,0,0,,There's no need \Nto obey these ridiculous orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.25,0:12:48.38,Main,L,0,0,0,,Run away.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.97,0:12:50.75,Italics,S,0,0,0,,To where?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.83,0:12:54.03,Italics,S,0,0,0,,Everyone dies someday.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.34,0:12:58.43,Italics,S,0,0,0,,You can't blame someone just\N because that day came a little early.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.43,0:13:03.61,Main,L,0,0,0,,Why do you always just accept it?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.24,0:13:05.78,Main,L,0,0,0,,You're losing your future, your wishes,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.78,0:13:07.79,Main,L,0,0,0,,even your life...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.27,0:13:12.82,Main,L,0,0,0,,And you don't hate us?\N How is that possible?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.52,0:13:18.85,Italics,S,0,0,0,,Major, we're not going to die.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.44,0:13:25.21,Italics,S,0,0,0,,We're finally following the path \Nwe wanted to follow,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.21,0:13:27.78,Italics,S,0,0,0,,to the place we wanted to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.48,0:13:30.71,Italics,S,0,0,0,,We can finally be free.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.71,0:13:32.85,Italics,S,0,0,0,,I would prefer you didn't disparage that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.42,0:13:37.55,Main,L,0,0,0,,Then... Then at least don't fight any more.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.89,0:13:38.87,Italics,S,0,0,0,,I have to.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.30,0:13:41.80,Italics,S,0,0,0,,We need to fight to go forward.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.44,0:13:46.71,Italics,S,0,0,0,,We've known it from the start.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.86,0:13:53.12,Main,L,0,0,0,,To kill your brother, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.51,0:13:59.12,Italics,S,0,0,0,,Why did you have to realize that?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.72,0:14:02.40,Main,L,0,0,0,,I can tell...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.40,0:14:05.66,Main,L,0,0,0,,You're sad, but you still laugh coldly
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.40,0:14:08.70,Main,L,0,0,0,,when you talk about your brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.26,0:14:12.05,Main,L,0,0,0,,Don't fight, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.05,0:14:14.56,Main,L,0,0,0,,Even if he's part of the Legion, \Nyou can't fight your brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.56,0:14:16.20,Italics,S,0,0,0,,My brother is a Shepherd.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.55,0:14:18.14,Italics,S,0,0,0,,I can't go anywhere without killing him.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.14,0:14:18.93,Main,L,0,0,0,,Captain!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.93,0:14:19.76,Italics,S,0,0,0,,Major...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.83,0:14:23.81,Italics,S,0,0,0,,There is no need to monitor us anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.81,0:14:24.69,Main,L,0,0,0,,Does that mean—
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.69,0:14:28.14,Italics,S,0,0,0,,I don't want you \Nto hear my brother's last words.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.75,0:14:31.68,Italics,S,0,0,0,,So please don't contact us again.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.14,0:14:40.12,Italics,S,0,0,0,,Go past the eastern border, \Nand you'll no longer hear the Legion's voices.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.68,0:14:44.35,Italics,S,0,0,0,,If anyone's left alive, help may come there.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.58,0:14:49.66,Italics,S,0,0,0,,When a Shepherd dies, \Nit throws the Legion into chaos for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.66,0:14:52.20,Italics,S,0,0,0,,We can buy you that much time.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.72,0:14:53.57,Italics,S,0,0,0,,So...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.62,0:14:55.95,Main,L,0,0,0,,Captain Nouzen...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.08,0:14:59.74,Italics,S,0,0,0,,Survive until then.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.43,0:15:20.98,Dates,S,0,0,0,,{\fad(487,478)}September 27th, Stellar Year 2148
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.93,0:15:29.95,Main,S,0,0,0,,Well?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.32,0:15:35.27,Main,Lef,0,0,0,,Provisions, fuel, ammo, \Nand spare parts are all packed.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.25,0:15:40.93,Main,Lef,0,0,0,,I also packed extra spares for the legs, \Nfor a certain idiot commander.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.93,0:15:42.52,Main,S,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.52,0:15:45.31,Main,Lef,0,0,0,,You can do simple repairs yourself, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.31,0:15:47.48,Main,S,0,0,0,,Yeah. I break them a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.48,0:15:50.42,Main,Lef,0,0,0,,Act a little ashamed, brat!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.72,0:15:53.09,Main,Lef,0,0,0,,Don't fight like you usually do.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.09,0:15:55.56,Main,S,0,0,0,,I can't promise.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.56,0:15:59.06,Main,Lef,0,0,0,,It's the last time, so just lie and agree.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.35,0:16:00.45,Main,S,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.03,0:16:02.10,Main,Lef,0,0,0,,Jeez...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.46,0:16:04.73,Main,Lef,0,0,0,,You really are...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.99,0:16:20.24,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,I feel bad for Haruto.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.24,0:16:23.93,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,If he'd lasted a little longer, \Nhe could've gone for a fun hike.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.93,0:16:24.97,Main,S,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.97,0:16:26.83,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Think the rain'll stop?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.83,0:16:29.71,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,It'd be nice to have clear skies, \Nat least for the first day.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.71,0:16:33.32,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,I know a trick! Kaie used to do it!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.32,0:16:35.67,Main,Lef,0,0,0,,Hey, kids! Come here.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.60,0:16:46.59,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Now that it's the last time, \NI realize I'm gonna miss the old guy's lectures.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.59,0:16:48.12,Main,All,0,0,0,,You think?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.39,0:17:50.30,Main,All,0,0,0,,Let's eat!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.79,0:17:54.80,sign_25674_247_September_28th__,All,0,0,0,,{\fad(488,477)}September 28th, Stellar Year 2148
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.24,0:17:55.73,Main Top,Kurena,0,0,0,,We all gathered here on the first day, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.73,0:17:56.83,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,You mean the day we were assigned here?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.83,0:17:57.59,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,Yup.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.59,0:18:03.19,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Yeah, we all swore to each other again.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.30,0:18:08.94,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,"No matter who calls us pigs, \Nwe'll never let ourselves become them."
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.27,0:18:14.49,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,"Even if we're the last one, \Nwe'll fight until the last day."
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.62,0:18:18.20,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,And all five of us survived.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.20,0:18:19.45,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Not bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.67,0:18:26.09,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,The Major never did call back.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.09,0:18:27.98,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,What, you miss her?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.98,0:18:29.13,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Not at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.51,0:18:32.76,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,I guess it does kind of bug me, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.76,0:18:36.72,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,After all the time we've spent together, \Nshe could've said goodbye.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.72,0:18:38.43,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Yeah, like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.43,0:18:42.82,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,We told her a million times to leave us alone, \Nand she finally got it, is all.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.36,0:18:46.84,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,The rain stopped.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.84,0:18:48.27,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,Clear skies!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.27,0:18:50.31,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,The trick worked, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.31,0:18:52.67,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,It's a good omen!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.27,0:18:54.37,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,Look, look!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.37,0:18:55.88,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,They're all shiny!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.88,0:18:58.14,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,I cleaned all your marks, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.35,0:19:00.65,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,You're nice and clean, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.65,0:19:02.31,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,How cool!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.62,0:19:03.77,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,He's happy?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.14,0:19:05.90,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,He was filthy.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.09,0:19:08.16,Main,S,0,0,0,,I'm happy for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.61,0:19:17.78,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,What's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.78,0:19:19.28,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,Snacks.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.28,0:19:20.51,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Is this...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.56,0:19:26.36,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,He treated us like kids until the end.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.52,0:19:34.26,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Nobody forgot anything, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.45,0:19:35.24,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,Nope!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.34,0:19:36.14,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Nope!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.36,0:19:37.07,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.31,0:19:39.11,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Shin.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.76,0:19:42.73,Main,S,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.96,0:21:42.27,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,I wanted to protect you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.09,0:21:45.33,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,That was how it was supposed to be, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.99,0:21:49.00,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,Shin.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.39,0:21:55.88,Flashback Top,S,0,0,0,,Brother, are Mom and Dad not coming back?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.33,0:21:57.30,Flashback Top,S,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.30,0:22:00.29,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,I could barely keep myself together back then.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.54,0:22:00.09,Flashback Top,S,0,0,0,,I can't hear Mom's voice.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.29,0:22:04.56,Flashback Top,S,0,0,0,,Brother, why did Mom die?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.33,0:22:07.88,Flashback Top,Rei,0,0,0,,It's your fault!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.36,0:22:08.33,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,That's not true.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.33,0:22:11.39,Flashback Top,Rei,0,0,0,,Mom went to fight because of you!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.89,0:22:11.68,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,That's not true.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.92,0:22:14.26,Flashback Top,Rei,0,0,0,,You killed her.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.26,0:22:14.89,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,Stop it!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.33,0:22:16.47,Flashback Top,Rei,0,0,0,,It's your fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.47,0:22:17.37,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,That's not true.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.37,0:22:20.10,Flashback Top,Rei,0,0,0,,It's all your fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.10,0:22:21.42,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,It's not your fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.42,0:22:24.90,Flashback Top,Rei,0,0,0,,That Mom and Dad died. \NThe fact that I'm about to die.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.90,0:22:28.11,Flashback Top,Rei,0,0,0,,It's all your fault,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.33,0:22:32.42,Flashback Top,Rei,0,0,0,,Shin!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.62,0:22:32.42,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.26,0:22:42.28,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,I couldn't handle the hate and rage \NI felt at my own powerlessness,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.83,0:22:45.20,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,and I took it out on you,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.51,0:22:48.16,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,the person I was supposed to protect.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.42,0:23:02.07,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,I couldn't protect you.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:03.21,0:23:03.99,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:06.03,0:23:07.10,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,Shin...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.58,0:23:13.85,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,Now we'll be together forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.85,0:23:17.42,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,I'm coming for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.93,0:23:20.46,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,Without my fragile human body.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.66,0:23:25.40,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,This time, \Nyour brother will protect you forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.04,0:23:28.12,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,So...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:30.11,0:23:33.75,Italics,Rei,0,0,0,,Come see me, Shin!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.31,0:23:37.52,Main,,0,0,0,,"Goodbye."
